# Code quality gate (Skin Studio — web)

Short guidance for front-end work. **Numeric thresholds below are guidance only** — this repo does not yet ship an analyser that enforces them. When ESLint / Biome / stylelint (or similar) lands, update this file to point at the real command and treat failing checks as blockers.

## Principles

- **KISS** — simplest design that meets the current need.
- **YAGNI** — only what the story requires; no hooks “for later”.
- **WET → DRY** — duplicating once is OK; factorize when the pattern is stable (~2nd–3rd time).
- **Boy Scout (scoped)** — improve the zone changed for the ticket; do **not** clean an entire large file because one line moved.
- **English everywhere** in code and UI strings (identifiers, comments that stay in source, user-visible product strings unless a future i18n story says otherwise).
- **Naming** — `camelCase` locals / functions; `PascalCase` components / classes / types; `UPPER_SNAKE` module-level constants; avoid Hungarian / cryptic abbreviations. Names must reveal intent (`loadSkin`, not `doStuff` / `process2`).
- **Names over narrative comments** — do not paper over a vague function with a comment that describes what it does; rename or extract instead. Comments only for *why* / non-obvious constraints, never as a substitute for a clear name.

## Thresholds (guidance — not auto-enforced yet)

| Metric | Guidance max |
|---|---|
| Function / method | ~40 lines (UI glue / handlers up to ~50 if still readable) |
| Parameters | 4 (group into an options object beyond that) |
| Nesting depth | 4 (prefer early returns / extract) |
| Useful source file | ~400 lines (split by responsibility when larger) |

Framework / browser APIs are not rewritten solely to satisfy parameter counts. Historical debt outside the diff is a separate chore.

## Front-end notes

- Prefer clear DOM / component boundaries over clever abstractions.
- Keep CSS specificity and global side effects under control in the touched zone; do not restyle the whole app “while here”.
- No phantom quality scripts: do **not** invent `lint_touched.py` or claim a C++-style analyser exists here.

## Definition of done

Before finishing a coding task:

1. The change does what the story / request asked — nothing more.
2. Relevant tests pass **when they exist**.
3. If a project linter / formatter is configured, run it on touched files and fix findings.
4. Until a linter exists: apply the principles and guidance thresholds above by eye on the diff; do **not** run a mandatory redesign loop.

**No** whole-file Boy Scout outside ticket scope. **Commits only when Guillaume explicitly asks.**
